{"type":"text","text":"Found all three HUD variables in Super Mario Bros. (World) World 1-1 by differential search, no reference used (everything below is internal RAM, `$0000-$07FF`; no ROM was written). A real game was started via Start → wait → Start, confirmed by a screenshot showing TIME 395 / score 000000 / coins x00.\n\n## 1. Coin count (displayed)\n**`$07ED` = tens, `$07EE` = ones — 2 BCD bytes.**\n\n- Differential: collecting the 1-1 ? block coin raised 264 addresses (`increased`, `c0`→`c1`) — Mario also moved, so that round is wide. Filtering that set by `equals 1` left **32**, including `$07EE` (0→1) and `$075E` (0→1).\n- Repeated the same coin after dying (coins persist): `equals 2` left **17**, including `$07EE` (1→2) and `$075E` (1→2). Intersection = `$07EE` and `$075E`.\n- **Proof:** wrote `$07ED/$07EE = [5,5]`, then collected one coin; the HUD redrew to **x56** (the written tens 5 appeared, the ones ticked 5→6) and RAM read back `[5,6]`.\n- Extent probe: wrote `$07EC..$07EF = [9,5,5,8]`, collected a coin; HUD showed only **x56** — the `9` and `8` neighbours are not displayed.\n\n## 2. Level timer (TIME)\n**`$07F8` = hundreds, `$07F9` = tens, `$07FA` = ones — 3 BCD bytes.**\n\n- Differential while Mario stood still (nothing but the timer and frame counters move): 150 idle frames, diff `decreased` left **21** survivors including `$07F9` (8→7) and `$07FA` (4→3). The second 150-frame round (`from: dt1`) left **6**: `$00F7`, `$00F8`, `$00F9`, `$07AC`, `$07B0`, `$07F9`.\n- Paused check: HUD read TIME 310 and RAM read exactly `[3,1,0]`.\n- **Proof:** wrote `$07F8-$07FA = [5,0,0]` (500); the game's own tick decremented it and the screenshot showed **TIME 499** (naturally it was at 099). The timer redraws its digits only on a tick.\n\n## 3. Score (MARIO)\n**`$07DD-$07E2` — 6 BCD bytes, most-significant first: `$07DD`=millions, `$07DE`=100k, `$07DF`=10k, `$07E0`=thousands, `$07E1`=hundreds, `$07E2`=tens; the HUD appends a fixed `0` ones tile (7 displayed digits).**\n\n- Differential: the ? block coin adds exactly 200. `equals 2` over the increased set left **15** including `$07E1` (0→2); the second coin (score 200→400) `equals 4` left **3** including `$07E1` (2→4) — the only address in both.\n- **Proof:** wrote `$07DD-$07E2 = [1,2,3,4,5,6]`, then collected a coin; the HUD redrew to **1234760** — my written digits appear and only the hundreds place moved 5→7 for the +200, read back as `[1,2,3,4,7,6]`.\n- Extent probe: wrote `$07DC..$07E4 = [9,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8]` and collected a coin; the nametable showed tiles `[1,2,3,4,7,6,0]` — `$07E3`=7 did **not** appear (the 7th digit stayed the fixed `0`), so the field is exactly `$07DD-$07E2`.\n\n## Also found\n**`$075E` — binary coin counter** (1 byte). Tracked 0→1→2 one-for-one with the displayed coins; wrote 7, collected a coin, read back 8. It is not drawn on the HUD (it drives the 1-UP at 100), so the HUD coin value is `$07ED/$07EE`.\n\nAll four were recorded with `record_mapping` (source \"differential search\") plus a note on the extent probes, and `promote_mappings` was called — the ROM's mapping file now has 12 addresses."}
